hadiths[58]{hadithnumber,text}:
"425","On the authority of Hazrat Abu Huraira, may Allah be pleased with him, the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: “Remember the destroyer of pleasures, i.e. death, often.”"
"426","Narrated by Hazrat Anas, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \None of you should wish for death because of the suffering that has befallen him.\"" And if it is necessary to desire it"","" then it should be said like this: O Allah! Keep me alive as long as life is good for me and let me die when death is better for me.” (Bukhari and Muslim)"""""
"427","It is narrated on the authority of Hazrat Burida, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \A believer dies with the sweat of his forehead.\"""""""
"428","On the authority of Hazrat Abu Saeed and Hazrat Abu Huraira, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Admonish your dead [La ilaha illa Allah].” (Narrated by Muslim and all four)."
"429","On the authority of Hazrat Muaqal bin Yasar, may Allah be pleased with him, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \Recite Surah Yassa near your dead.\"""""""
"430","It was narrated from Hazrat Umm Salamah that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, came at the time of the death of Hazrat Abu Salamah, and his eyes were open at that time. He closed it and then said: \When the soul is seized"","" the eye follows it.\"" (Hearing this) the people of the house started crying and shouting out of panic and worry"","" so he said: \""Do not say anything except good and better dua for yourself"","" because the angels say Amen to what you say.\"" Then he prayed: \""O God! Forgive Abu Salama (may God be pleased with him)"","" raise his status among the guided people"","" widen his grave"","" enlighten him"","" and make him a vicegerent among those who live behind him.” (Narrated by Muslim)"""""
"431","It was narrated from Hazrat Aisha that when the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) died, he was covered with a striped cloak. (Bukhari and Muslim)"
"432","It was narrated from Hazrat Aisha that Hazrat Abu Bakr kissed the Prophet's (forehead) after his death. (Narrated by Bukhari.)"
"433","On the authority of Hazrat Abu Hurairah, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \The soul of a believer hangs because of his debt"","" even if it is paid off by him.\"""""""
"434","On the authority of Hazrat Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said about the man who fell off his horse and died: \Ghusl him with water and berry (leaves) and shroud him in both his (Ihram) clothes.\"" (Bukhari and Muslim)."""""
"435","It was narrated from Hazrat Aisha (RA) that when the Companions (RA) decided to bathe the Messenger of Allah (PBUH), they said: By Allah! We do not know whether we should take off the clothes of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, as we take off the clothes of our dead or not. This is a long hadith. (Narrated by Ahmad and Abu Dawood.)"
"436","Hazrat Umm Atiya (RA) narrated that the Prophet (PBUH) came to us while we were bathing his daughter. He said: \Give him a bath three or five times\"" or more \""if you feel the need\"" with water in which berry leaves have been mixed and add camphor in the last time"","" or he said"","" add some camphor. It is: \""Start the ablution from their right sides and limbs.\"" In a tradition of Bukhari: We tied the hair of their heads into three braids and placed them on their backs."""""
"437","It was narrated from Hazrat Aisha that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, was shrouded in three white cloths made by Suhliya Basti, which were made of cotton and did not have a shirt or turban. (Bukhari and Muslim)"
"438","Hazrat Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that when Abdullah bin Abi (the hypocrite) died, his son (Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him)) came to the service of the Messenger of Allah (may peace be upon him) and asked him to give me his shirt so that I may shroud him in it. So he gave him his shirt. (Bukhari and Muslim)"
"439","On the authority of Hazrat Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \Put on a white garment among your clothes"","" for it is the best and noblest of all your garments.\"" And shroud your dead in it.”"""""
"440","On the authority of Hazrat Jabir, may Allah be pleased with him, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \When one of you gives a shroud to his brother"","" he should give him a good shroud.\"" (Narrated by Muslim)."""""
"441","It was narrated from Hazrat Jabir that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to gather two men from the martyrs of Uhud together in one cloth (shroud) and inquire: \Which of them remembered the Qur'an more?\"" Neither these martyrs were bathed nor their funeral prayers were offered. (Narrated by Bukhari.)"""""
"442","Hazrat Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: \Do not give (your dead) precious shrouds"","" for they are soon taken away.\"" (Narrated by Abu Dawood.)"""""
"443","Hazrat Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to her: \If you die before me"","" I will bathe you.\"" This is a long hadith. (Narrated by Ahmad and Ibn Majah and authenticated by Ibn Hibban.)"""""
"444","It was narrated from Hazrat Asmaa bint Umays (RA) that Hazrat Fatima (RA) had bequeathed that Hazrat Ali (RA) herself should bathe her. (Narrated by Darqutani.)"
"445","It is narrated from Hadhrat Baridah in the story of Ghamdiyyah that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered stoning for committing adultery. They say: You ordered about it (funeral prayer), then you yourself offered his funeral prayer and he was buried. (Narrated by Muslim.)"
"446","It was narrated from Hazrat Jabir bin Samrah (RA) that a man was brought to the service of the Prophet (PBUH) who had committed suicide with a broad spear. You did not pray for him. (Narrated by Muslim.)"
"447","It is narrated from Hazrat Abu Huraira (RA) about this woman who used to sweep the mosque. He said: \Why didn't you inform me?\"" as if he considered the matter of his death trivial. He said: \""Tell me his grave.\"" The Companions told him the grave. So he offered his funeral prayer. (Bukhari and Muslim) And Muslim has narrated so much that he then said: \""These graves are full of darkness for the people of the graves and Allah makes their graves bright for them through my prayer.\"""""""
"448","It was narrated from Hazrat Hudhayfah that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to forbid Na'i (public proclamation of death). (It was narrated by Ahmad and Tirmidhi and Tirmidhi declared it hasan.)"
"449","It was narrated on the authority of Hazrat Abu Huraira that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave the news of the death of Najashi on the same day that he died. He took the Companions and went to the funeral home, lined them up and recited four takbirs on it. (Bukhari and Muslim)"
"450","It was narrated from Hazrat Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, that I heard the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, say: “If there are forty people present at the funeral of a Muslim who do not associate anything with Allah, then Allah accepts their intercession for him (the deceased).” (Narrated by Muslim)."
"451","It was narrated from Hazrat Samura bin Jundab (RA) that I prayed the funeral prayer behind the Prophet (PBUH) for a woman who had died in childbirth. You stood in the middle of it. (Bukhari and Muslim)"
"452","It was narrated from Hazrat Aisha that by Allah! The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed the funeral prayers of Baida's two sons in the mosque. (Narrated by Muslim.)"
"453","It was narrated from Hazrat Abdul Rahman bin Abi Laila (may God have mercy on him) that Hazrat Zayd bin Arqam (may Allah be pleased with him) used to say four takbirs at our funerals. (But against the norm) Once he recited five takbirs, I asked him. He replied that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say five takbeers. (Narrated by Muslim and the four)."
"454","It is narrated from Hazrat Ali (RA) that he recited six takbirs in the funeral prayer of Hazrat Sahl bin Hanif (RA) and said that these are Badri. (Narrated by Saeed bin Mansur and its original is in Bukhari.)"
"455","It was narrated from Hazrat Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say four takbeers at our funerals and in the first takbeer he would recite Surah Fatiha. (It was narrated by Imam Shafi'i, may God have mercy on him, with a weak chain of transmission.)"
"456","It was narrated from Hazrat Talha bin Abdullah bin Auf, may God have mercy on him, that I offered the funeral prayer behind Hazrat Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him. He recited Surah Al-Fatiha in it and said: (I have recited Surah Al-Fatiha for this reason) so that you may know that this is a Sunnah. (Narrated by Bukhari.)"
"457","It was narrated from Hazrat Awf bin Malik that the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, led a funeral prayer, so I remembered this part of his prayer: [Allahum! ... and the torment of the fire] \O Allah! Forgive him and have mercy on him. And grant him peace and forgive him. Give him good hospitality. Make his grave spacious and generous. Wash it with water"","" snow and hail (make it completely clean). And grant him a house better than this (worldly) house and a family better than his family. Enter him into Paradise. Protect him from the trials and tribulations of the grave and the punishment of hell.” (Narrated by Muslim)"""""
"458","Hazrat Abu Huraira (RA) narrated that the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) used to say: Forgive and pardon our living and dead, our present and absent, our young and old, our men and women. God! Whoever of us you keep alive, keep him alive on Islam, and whoever you kill, let him be proud of the death of faith. God! Not depriving us of the rewards and rewards of this (deceased) and not putting us into temptation after that.” (Narrated by Muslim and the four)."
"459","On the authority of Hazrat Abu Hurairah, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \When you offer the funeral prayer for a dead person"","" pray for him sincerely.\"" (Narrated by Abu Dawud and authenticated by Ibn Habban)."""""
"460","On the authority of Hazrat Abu Huraira, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \Do you hasten to carry the funeral"","" because if it is good"","" then it is good to which you are taking it"","" and if it is not good"","" then it is evil that you are removing from your neck.\"" (Bukhari and Muslim)."""""
"461","On the authority of Hazrat Abu Huraira, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \Whoever stays with the funeral until the prayer is offered"","" he will receive a reward equal to one carat.\"" And the person who remains present until the burial will be rewarded with two carats. He said: \""Two carats are equal to two big mountains.\"" (Bukhari and Muslim) And it is in the tradition of Muslim: \""He was present until the deceased was lowered into the grave.\"" And it is in the tradition of Bukhari: \""Whoever attended the funeral of a Muslim in a state of faith and with the intention of obtaining reward and stayed with him until the end of the funeral prayer and returned after leaving the burial"","" then he returned with two carats.\"" Each carat is equal to the weight of Mount Uhud."""""
"462","Hazrat Salim (may Allah have mercy on him) narrates from his father (Ibn Umar) that he saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and Hazrat Abu Bakr Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) walking in front of the funeral. (It has been narrated by all five and Ibn Hibban has declared it to be Sahih. And Nasa'i and a group have explained the reason for its transmission in it.)"
"463","It was narrated from Hazrat Umm Atiya (RA) that we were forbidden to attend funerals, but no firm order was given. (Bukhari and Muslim)"
"464","On the authority of Hazrat Abu Saeed, may Allah be pleased with him, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \When you see a funeral procession"","" stand up"",""\"" and whoever is with the funeral procession should not sit before the funeral procession is placed (on the ground).\"" (Bukhari and Muslim)."""""
"465","It was narrated from Hazrat Abu Ishaq, may God have mercy on him, that Hazrat Abdullah bin Yazid, may Allah be pleased with him, lowered the deceased into the grave from the bottom of the grave and said that this is the Sunnah method. (It was narrated by Abu Dawud.)"
"466","Narrated by Hazrat Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with him: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “When you lower your dead into the graves, say: [In the name of Allah and the religion of the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace].” has declared it as Sahih, while Daraqtani has declared it to be Maaalul and has called it Muqoof.)"
"467","Hazrat Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (may peace be upon him) said: “Breaking the bones of a dead person is like breaking the bones of a living person.”"
"468","On the authority of Hazrat Saad bin Abi Waqqas, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: For me, to build a lahd-wali, meaning a grave by the side, and to choose raw bricks over it, as was done with the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace. (It was narrated by Muslim.) And Bayhaqi narrated the same narration regarding Hazrat Jabir (RA) and added so much that his grave was made only one pillow high above the ground. (It is declared authentic by Ibn Hibban.) And it was narrated in Muslim on the authority of Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the grave to be paved and to sit on it and to build a building on it."
"469","It was narrated from Hazrat Aamir bin Rabi'ah that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) offered the funeral prayer of Uthman bin Maza'un (may Allah be pleased with him) and visited his grave and placed three laps of dust while standing. (Narrated by Darqutani.)"
"470","It was narrated from Hazrat Uthman (may Allah be pleased with him) that when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) finished burying the dead, he would stand at the grave (by the grave) and say: “Ask for forgiveness for your brother and pray for steadfastness because now he will be interrogated.”"
"471","Hazrat Zamra bin Habib, may God have mercy on him, who is a follower. It has been narrated that people used to think it is recommended that when the grave of the deceased is leveled and leveled and people start leaving, they should stand near the grave and address the deceased and say: O So-and-so! Say there is no god but Allah. Say it three times. O so-and-so! Say: [Rabbi-Allah wa-deeni-i-Islamu wa-nabi-i-Muhammad] “My Lord is Allah, my religion is Islam, and Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace, is my Prophet.”"
"472","It is narrated from Hazrat Barida bin Hasib Aslami, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \I forbade you from visiting the graves.\"" Now visit them.\"" (Narrated by Muslim.) Tirmidhi has quoted this addition: \""Because visiting the graves reminds you of the Hereafter.\"" And Ibn Majah has described this addition in a hadith narrated by Hazrat Ibn Mas'ud"","" may Allah be pleased with him: \""This visit makes you disinterested in the world.\"""""""
"473","It was narrated from Hazrat Abu Hurairah that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, cursed women who went to visit graves. (Narrated by Tirmidhi and declared authentic by Ibn Hibban.)"
"474","It was narrated from Hazrat Abu Saeed Al-Khudri (RA) that the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) cursed the one who mourns and the one who listens. (It was narrated by Abu Dawud.)"
"475","Hazrat Umm Atiya (may Allah be pleased with her) narrated that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took a pledge from us that we would not mourn over the dead. (Bukhari and Muslim)"
"476","On the authority of Hazrat Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “A person who dies is punished in his grave because he is mourned over him.”"
"477","Hazrat Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) reported that I was present at the burial of one of the daughters of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was sitting near the grave. I saw tears flowing from both your eyes. (Narrated by Bukhari.)"
"478","On the authority of Hazrat Jabir, may Allah be pleased with him, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \Do not bury your dead at night unless you are forced to do so.\"""""""
"479","On the authority of Hazrat Abdullah bin Jafar, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: When the news of the martyrdom of Jafar (bin Abi Talib) was received, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \Prepare food for the family of Jafar"","" for something has come to them that has distracted them (from cooking).\"""""""
"480","Hazrat Sulaiman bin Burida, may God have mercy on him, narrates from his father that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to teach his companions that when they go to the graveyard, they should say: \Peace be upon you"","" O householders!\"" Among the believers and Muslims. And we are also going to meet you"","" God willing. And we ask Allah for peace for us and you.” (Narrated by Muslim)"""""
"481","It was narrated from Hazrat Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, passed through the graveyard of Medina. He turned to them and said: \O people of the graves! Peace be upon you. May Allah forgive us and you. You are our forerunner and we are following you."""""
"482","On the authority of Hazrat Aisha, she narrates that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \Do not speak ill of men"","" for whatever they sent forward has reached him.\"" By saying) you will hurt the living.''"""""
